  "laneNotes": [
    "AOC-334 is the order the judge signs, not the filing, and it prints both KRS 218A.275 and KRS 218A.276 on its own face. One form serves both families, and the assignment's officialFormFamily is correct for this lane.",
    "The proposed order is filled in the shared field semantics' caption mode and in no other mode: the style of the case only. Five caption facts are written; the recitals, the completion date, the charges, the agency list, the ordering date, the judge's signature and the agency certification block are all left as the court printed them.",
    "Nothing this build holds establishes who must be served with this motion or by what method. The certificate of service names no recipient, states no method, declares both required-before-filing and discloses them; the instructions say the circuit court clerk is who to ask. No recipient and no method was guessed, and no BLOCKED_LEGAL_INPUT row is written for it because it is a fact to collect rather than a legal question to answer.",
    "The completion date appears on both the motion and the tendered order. It is disclosed on each and the instructions say in terms to write the same date in both places."
  ],
